  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Clinical History - Mrs. \xC2ngela Lopes\n \nMrs. \xC2ngela Lopes, 66 years
    old, suffers from chronic renal failure with 2 hemodialysis sessions per week.
    She was hospitalized for a week in the general medicine department of a French-speaking
    hospital. She is of French origin, retired from the restaurant business, and
    lives in a small village 30 km from the hospital. \nShe is married, mother of
    3 children, 2 of whom are still under her care. Mrs. \xC2ngela likes to take
    care of her vegetable garden, watch television and meet her friends. She frequently
    visits Brittany, where she has family. She particularly likes the local cuisine
    - rich in fish, seafood and charcuterie - that her husband prepares for the family.
    She has a clean appearance and good personal hygiene. She is 1.67m tall and weighs
    67kg. \nBackground / Medical History \n\u25CF Smoker since the age of 14.\r\n\u25CF
    Left ventricular failure, and hypertension since 1999.\r\n\u25CF Chronic renal
    failure (secondary to chronic glomerulonephritis and nephroangiosclerosis) diagnosed
    in 2012, with partially preserved diuresis until June 2016.\n\r\nHistory of the
    disease\r\nMrs. \xC2ngela Lopes has been known to the nephrology department since
    September 12, 2014.\r\nDuring this first hospitalization, she started hemodialysis
    (HD), and a Cimino-Brescia arteriovenous fistula (AVF) was created in her left
    forearm. The discharge treatment prescribed by the nephrologist was 3 sessions
    of 4 hours of HD per week, at the hospital's dialysis center, which involved
    quite long travel times... \nThe patient and her husband refused to submit to
    such restrictions; the Mrs. verbalizes that the disease takes up too much space
    in her daily life, and some life goals had to be revised related to the restrictions
    imposed by this disease. The treatment was finally reduced to:\r\n\u25CF 2 hemodialysis
    sessions per week, of 5 hours each.\r\n\u25CF A medical treatment.\r\n\u25CF
    LASIX\xAE 2 x 40mg PO per day.\r\n\u25CF RENITEN\xAE 1 x 20mg PO per day.\r\n\u25CF
    A diet with fluid restrictions to 1 liter per day"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2e498d1c8094910479dc3e1b768306a4, type: 2}
